#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:3
msgid "AMDGPU Memory Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:6
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:8
msgid ""
"The {ref}`LLVM memory model<memmodel>` provides broad guarantees that are "
"sufficient to implement inter-thread communication via memory. But in most "
"communication patterns, not all memory accesses performed by a thread need "
"to be exposed to other threads. Even when they do need to be exposed, not "
"all threads may need to observe these memory accesses. This document "
"describes the *AMDGPU memory model* that allows the user to control how the "
"side-effects of memory accesses are propagated across threads. The "
"programmer expresses this using **new intrinsics and metadata** as described "
"below, and the implementation can then choose a more efficient mechanism to "
"complete them, such as the cache policy bits in an AMDGPU device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:19
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model allows executions that are not allowed by the LLVM "
"memory model. At the same time, a simple mapping can be used to implement "
"these new intrinsics and metadata using operations defined in the default "
"LLVM memory model. Thus, **there exists a safe-by-default implementation** "
"that produces executions that are valid in both models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:25
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:27
msgid "Memory Accesses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:29
msgid ""
"Operations that read or write locations in memory are termed as *memory "
"accesses*. Typical examples are `load`, `store` and atomic instructions, as "
"well as many intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:33
msgid "Synchronizing Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:35
msgid ""
"Synchronizing operations control how the side-effects of memory accesses are "
"propagated in the system. Typical examples are atomic operations (including "
"fences) with at least `release` or `acquire` ordering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:41
msgid "Scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:43
msgid ""
"A *scope* is an abstract description of sets of memory accesses and "
"synchronizing operations in a multi-threaded execution environment. Each "
"such set is called an *instance* of that scope, or a *scope instance* for "
"short."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:47
msgid ""
"Each memory access or synchronizing operation belongs to at most one "
"instance of every scope defined by the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:49
msgid ""
"When an operation `X` specifies a scope `S`, it indicates the instance of "
"`S` that contains `X`. This scope instance is also termed as *X's instance "
"of scope S*, or just *X's scope instance* when `S` is implied by the context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:53
msgid ""
"When an operation does not specify a scope, it indicates the *system* scope "
"defined below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:56
msgid "LLVM scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:58
msgid ""
"The LLVM Language Reference defines the following {ref}`scopes<syncscope>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:60
msgid "*system scope* (empty string \"\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:62
msgid ""
"There exists a single instance of this scope that contains the memory "
"accesses and synchronizing operations performed by all threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:65
msgid "\"singlethread\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:67
msgid ""
"Each thread corresponds to a \"singlethread\" scope instance that contains "
"the memory accesses and synchronizing operations performed by that thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:70
msgid "AMDGPU scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:72
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU backend further refines the LLVM scopes with the following target-"
"defined scopes and constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:75
msgid "*system scope* (same as LLVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:76
msgid "\"agent\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:77
msgid "\"cluster\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:78
msgid "\"workgroup\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:79
msgid "\"wavefront\" scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:80
msgid "\"singlethread\" scope (same as LLVM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:82
msgid ""
"These are arranged from largest scope (*system scope*) to smallest scope "
"(\"singlethread\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:85
msgid ""
"Every instance `X` of some scope `S1` other than \"singlethread\" scope is "
"partitioned by the scope `S2` one level below it. Each subset defined by "
"this partition is an instance of `S2` and is called a *subscope instance* of "
"`X`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:88
msgid ""
"It follows that if two scope instances `X` and `Y` intersect, then their "
"intersection is the smaller of `X` and `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:90
msgid ""
"A scope `S1` is a *subscope* of a scope `S2` if every instance of `S1` is a "
"subscope instance of some instance of `S2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:93
msgid ""
"**Inclusive Scopes**: Two operations `X` and `Y` are said to have *inclusive "
"scopes* if the scope instance of each operation contains the other "
"operation. In that case, the *common scope instance* `S'` of `X` and `Y` is "
"the intersection of their scope instances. The scope corresponding to `S'` "
"is also termed as the *common scope* of `X` and `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:99
msgid "Availability and Visibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:101
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model is built on top of the {ref}`happens-"
"before<memmodel>` order defined by the LLVM memory model. But when one of "
"the new intrinsics or metadata is used, **happens-before by itself is not "
"sufficient** to describe its observable effects. Instead, the AMDGPU model "
"uses *availability* and *visibility* to describe how the side-effects of "
"these operations propagate to other threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:108
msgid ""
"Availability determines how *far* the side-effects of a write have been "
"forwarded in the system relative to that write. Visibility determines how "
"*close* the side-effects of the same write have reached relative to an "
"observer operation (typically a read)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:113
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model *does not change the structure of happens-before*, "
"but changes the rules that determine how operations may observe the side-"
"effects of other operations that *happen-before* them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:117
msgid ""
"Consider a write `W` that `happens-before` a read `R` to the same address:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:119
msgid ""
"`R` can potentially observe the side-effects of `W` **only if W is visible** "
"to `R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:121
msgid ""
"`W` can potentially be visible to `R` **only if W is first made available** "
"to `R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:124
msgid ""
"The instructions used in the default LLVM memory model automatically satisfy "
"these necessary conditions, and hence they can be explained using the rules "
"from either memory model. But the new intrinsics and metadata *opt out* of "
"the LLVM memory model, and can only be explained using the AMDGPU memory "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:130
msgid ""
"We introduce new intrinsics because metadata cannot be used to express the "
"availability and visibility of ordinary load/store operations, because the "
"scope is necessary for correctness. In a hypothetical operation like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:139
msgid ""
"If the metadata is dropped or ignored, there is no guarantee that the store "
"will become available at the intended scope. In implementation terms, the "
"store may be completed at a nearer cache than the one required for that "
"scope. A corresponding *load-visible* that does not access the same near "
"cache will fail to observe this store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:148
msgid "store-available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:150
msgid ""
"A *store-available* operation `X` writes data to the specified location, and "
"then propagates those side-effects up to its scope instance `S` and also all "
"the subscope instances of `S` that contain `X`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:158
msgid ""
"The `@llvm.amdgcn.av.store.b128` intrinsic performs a non-atomic *store-"
"available* operation on `%addr` with scope `!scope`. See {ref}`amdgpu-av-"
"load-store` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:168
msgid ""
"An atomic operation that results in a store operation is a *store-available* "
"operation with scope `syncscope`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:173
msgid "load-visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:175
msgid ""
"A *load-visible* operation `Y` retrieves the state of the specified location "
"from its scope instance `S`, and then loads the value at that location. In "
"addition, it makes the retrieved state visible to all subscope instances of "
"`S` that contain `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:184
msgid ""
"The `@llvm.amdgcn.av.load.b128` intrinsic performs a non-atomic *load-"
"visible* operation on `%addr` with scope `!scope`. See {ref}`amdgpu-av-load-"
"store` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:194
msgid ""
"An atomic operation that results in a read operation is a *load-visible* "
"operation with scope `syncscope`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:197
msgid "addrspace(3) Accesses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:199
msgid ""
"Any access to `addrspace(3)` (aka LDS or local) always results in a *store-"
"available* or *load-visible* operation with scope \"workgroup\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:202
msgid ""
"Any access to `addrspace(0)` (aka flat or global) always results in a *store-"
"available* or *load-visible* operation with scope \"workgroup\", if the flat "
"address resolves to `addrspace(3)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:207
msgid ""
"This is independent of the `syncscope` of an atomic access. For example, "
"even if a `store atomic` to `addrspace(3)` specifies a smaller `syncscope` "
"such as \"wavefront\", the side-effects are made available at \"workgroup\" "
"scope. In other words, the scope for atomicity is not always the same as the "
"scope for availability/visibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:215
msgid "!\"amdgcn-av\" metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:221
msgid ""
"The presence of this metadata removes the ability of synchronizing "
"operations to establish availability and visibility, and essentially creates "
"*non-av* synchronizing operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:225
msgid ""
"For a synchronizing operation which itself accesses memory (e.g., `store "
"atomic release` or `load atomic acquire`), the metadata does not affect the "
"availability or the visibility of the access performed by the operation "
"itself. It only affects the synchronization of other memory accesses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:230
msgid "make-available and make-visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:232
msgid ""
"*make-available* and *make-visible* operations propagate certain side-"
"effects from or to the specified scope respectively. They are similar to the "
"*store-available* and *load-visible* operations, except that their effect is "
"not limited to specific locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:245
msgid ""
"A synchronizing operation with at least `release` ordering is a *make-"
"available* operation with scope `syncscope`, if it is not marked as `!{!"
"\"amdgcn-av\", !\"none\"}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:249
msgid ""
"A synchronizing operation with at least `acquire` ordering is a *make-"
"visible* operation with scope `syncscope`, if it is not marked as `!{!"
"\"amdgcn-av\", !\"none\"}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:267
msgid "Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:270
msgid ""
"**TODO:** These ordering operations affect all address spaces. We need to "
"eventually make that a parameter similar to the storage class parameter on "
"operations and orders in Vulkan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:275
msgid "Availability Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:277
msgid ""
"An operation `X` is an *availability operation* on a write `W` if one of the "
"following holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:280
msgid "`X` is `W` itself, and `W` is a *store-available* operation, or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:282
msgid ""
"`X` is a *make-available* operation that follows `W` in program order, or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:285
msgid ""
"`X` is a *make-available* operation whose scope instance includes `W`, and "
"there is an availability operation `Z` on `W` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:288
msgid "`Z` happens-before `X`, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:289
msgid "`Z`'s scope instance includes `X`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:291
msgid ""
"Then `X` makes `W` available in its own scope instance `S` and every "
"subscope instance of `S` that also includes `W`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:294
msgid "Visibility Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:296
msgid ""
"An operation `Y` is a *visibility operation* on a write `W` if `Y` is a "
"*load-visible* operation to the same address, or a *make-visible* operation, "
"and one of the following holds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:300
msgid "There exists an *availability* operation `X` on write `W` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:302 ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:310
msgid "`X` happens-before `Y`, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:303
msgid "`X` and `Y` have inclusive scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:305
msgid ""
"Then `Y` makes `W` visible in the common scope instance `S` of `X` and `Y`, "
"and every subscope instance of `S` that includes `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:308
msgid "There exists a *visibility* operation `X` on write `W` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:311
msgid "`X` makes `W` visible in a scope instance `S1` that includes `Y`, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:312
msgid "`X` is included in the scope instance `S2` of `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:314
msgid ""
"Then `Y` makes `W` visible in the intersection `S` of `S1` and `S2`, and "
"every subscope instance of `S` that includes `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:317
msgid "Location Order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:319
msgid ""
"A write `W` is *location-ordered* before an access `Y` to the same address "
"if `W` is program-ordered before `Y`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:322
msgid ""
"A write `W` is *location-ordered* before a write `W1` to the same address if "
"there exists an availability operation `Z` on `W` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:325
msgid "`Z` happens-before `W1`, and,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:326
msgid "`W1` is included in `Z`'s scope instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:328
msgid ""
"A write `W` is *location-ordered* before a read `R` to the same address if "
"there exists a visibility operation `Z` on write `W` such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:331
msgid "`Z` is `R` itself, or,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:332
msgid "`Z` precedes `R` in program order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:334
msgid ""
"A read `R` is *location-ordered* before an access (read and/or write) `X` to "
"the same address if it happens-before `X`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:337
msgid ""
"The AMDGPU memory model overrides the definition of each byte in the {ref}"
"`LLVM memory model<memmodel>` as follows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:340
msgid ""
"Every (defined) read operation `R` reads a series of bytes written by "
"(defined) write operations. Each initialized global is assumed to have an "
"initial *system scoped* atomic write operation that is *location-ordered* "
"before any other read or write to that same location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:345
msgid ""
"For each byte of a read `R`, `R` may see any write to the same byte, except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:347
msgid ""
"If a write `W1` is *location-ordered* before a write `W2`, and `W2` is "
"*location-ordered* before a read `R`, then `R` may not see `W1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:349
msgid ""
"If a read `R` is *location-ordered* before a write `W3`, then `R` may not "
"see `W3`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:352
msgid "The value returned by `R` is then defined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:354
msgid ""
"If no write is *location-ordered* before a read `R`, then `R` returns "
"`undef`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:356
msgid ""
"Otherwise if the set consisting of `R` and all writes that `R` may see "
"contains only atomic operations with inclusive scopes, then `R` returns the "
"value written by one of those writes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:359
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if `R` may see some write that is not *location-ordered* before "
"`R`, then `R` returns `undef`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:361
msgid ""
"Otherwise, if `R` may see exactly one write `W`, then `R` returns the value "
"written by `W`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:363
msgid "Otherwise, `R` returns `undef`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:365
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:368
msgid "This section is informational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:371
msgid "The following properties follow from the definitions above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:373
msgid ""
"**Happens-before is necessary for location-order.** An access `X` is "
"*location-ordered* before an access `Y` only if `X` happens-before `Y`. This "
"follows from the definition of availability and visibility operations, which "
"always require a happens-before link with the preceding operation in the "
"chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:378
msgid ""
"**A write cannot be made available in a scope that does not contain it.** "
"The definition of an availability operation `X` requires that `X`'s scope "
"instance includes `W` as a precondition. Since every scope instance that "
"includes `X` also includes `W`, availability cannot reach a scope instance "
"that excludes `W`. In other words, availability can only \"expand outwards\" "
"into progressively larger scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:384
msgid ""
"**Visibility is bounded by availability.** When a write is available in a "
"scope instance, it can be made visible in that scope instance by a "
"visibility operation with the corresponding scope. Subsequent *make-visible* "
"operations make that write visible into narrower scope instances towards the "
"observer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:388
msgid ""
"**A write can be made visible in a scope instance that does not contain it."
"** The definition of a *visibility operation* anchors scope instances to the "
"observer (`Y`), not to the original write. The only precondition is that the "
"write must already be visible or available in the scope instance of the "
"visibility operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUMemoryModel.md:393
msgid ""
"**Availability and visibility chains.** For a write `W` to be visible to a "
"read `R` anywhere in the system, the sufficient condition is a chain of "
"happens-before edges that include availability and visibility operations "
"with inclusive scopes. It is not necessary that `W` and `R` themselves have "
"inclusive scopes. Each link in the availability and visibility definitions "
"only checks the immediate predecessor, so intermediate operations can bridge "
"scope gaps that the endpoints cannot satisfy directly. Such a chain passes "
"through at least one availability operation and at least one visibility "
"operation with inclusive scopes, such that their common scope includes both "
"`W` and `R`."
msgstr ""

